\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Blender visualization of the synthetic 13-camera light field array. It consists of one central reference camera and twelve surrounding cameras arranged in a cross-shaped configuration with equal spacing.}}{20}{figure.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Blender scene used for the initial target-based calibration. The checkerboard pattern, placed at varying positions and orientations in front of the camera array, serves as the calibration target for estimating intrinsic and extrinsic parameters.}}{21}{figure.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Blender scene used for LiFCal-based recalibration without a calibration target. The scene contains multiple objects with diverse colors, textures, and lighting conditions to provide rich visual features and depth variation, enabling robust feature detection.}}{21}{figure.13}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Absolute deviation of the estimated focal lengths from ground truth for all cameras in the initial calibration. The blue curve represents the deviation of $f_x$, while the orange curve represents the deviation of $f_y$, both measured in pixels. A horizontal zero line indicates perfect agreement with the ground-truth parameters.}}{24}{figure.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Relative focal length error of $f_x$ for all cameras in the initial calibration, computed as $\frac {f_{\mathrm {est}} - f_{\mathrm {gt}}}{f_{\mathrm {gt}}} \cdot 100\%$. The plot shows the normalized percentage deviation with respect to the ground-truth focal length, allowing a scale-independent interpretation of the estimation accuracy.}}{24}{figure.15}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Absolute deviation of the estimated principal point coordinates from ground truth for all cameras in the initial calibration. The green curve represents the deviation of $c_x$, while the red dashed curve represents the deviation of $c_y$, both measured in pixels. The horizontal zero line indicates perfect agreement with the ground-truth values.}}{25}{figure.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Ground-truth 3D positions of all cameras in the synthetic multi-camera array. The plot shows the spatial arrangement of the cameras in the $(X, Y, Z)$ coordinate system, illustrating the cross-shaped configuration used for the simulation.}}{26}{figure.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Comparison of ground-truth and estimated camera positions after the initial calibration. Black markers represent the ground-truth positions, while magenta markers indicate the calibrated positions. The spatial overlap illustrates the translation estimation accuracy, with a reported mean position error of 0.028m.}}{26}{figure.18}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Rotation error per camera after the initial calibration. The bars represent the angular deviation between the estimated and ground-truth extrinsic rotations, measured in degrees. The dashed horizontal line indicates the mean rotation error across all cameras ($\emptyset = 0.11^\circ $).}}{27}{figure.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Absolute translation error per camera after the initial calibration. The bars represent the Euclidean distance between the estimated and ground-truth camera positions, measured in meters. The dashed horizontal line indicates the mean translation error across all cameras ($\emptyset = 0.028\,\text {m}$).}}{27}{figure.20}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Reprojection error per camera of the initial calibration.}}{28}{figure.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Stereo RMS error of the initial calibration.}}{28}{figure.22}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Reprojection error per camera for a single LiFCal-based recalibration run.}}{30}{figure.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces Reprojection error per camera across three LiFCal-based recalibration runs.}}{30}{figure.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {25}{\ignorespaces Comparison of mean reprojection error per camera between initial calibration and LiFCal-based recalibration. The blue curve corresponds to the one shown in \autoref {fig:reprojection_error_plot} and the orange curve corresponds to the one shown in \autoref {fig:lifcal_reprojection_error_1}.}}{31}{figure.25}%
